<title>UK: NWE high sulphur straight-run fuel oil firm.</title>
<headline>NWE high sulphur straight-run fuel oil firm.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>NWE high sulphur straight-run fuel oil was firmer on Friday as crude futures gained ground but dealers said they saw signs of improving supplies.</p>
<p>An ARA dealer was heard having bought a Russian cargo for the barge market. The price was p+c.</p>
<p>Traders offered M-40 cargoes at around $114 cif NWE but no other trade was heard done.</p>
<p>Low sulphur straight-run markets were becalmed and buyers and sellers were heard around $10 a tonne apart.</p>
<p>-- Nicholas Shaxson, London newsroom +44 171 542 8167</p>
